WEBVTT

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:02.540
Ordinary relationships are not automatically

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.660
inherited from the parent.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.800
Wait, really? So if I spend

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.420
an hour defining that a base

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.340
product has a complex relationship

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.620
to a supplier database, my newly

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.280
created frozen product doesn't just

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.780
automatically inherit that supplier

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.180
relationship? Not currently.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.060
No, you have to explicitly redefine

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.460
or map that relationship for the

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:22.960
derived type.
